<title>USA: KPMG Intl names Colin Sharman as chairman.</title>
<headline>KPMG Intl names Colin Sharman as chairman.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>KPMG International on Wednesday said it named Colin Sharman, senior partner of the firm's U.K. practice, as its new chairman.</p>
<p>Sharman succeeds Jon Madonna, who steps down January 31 from the post of international chairman, a position he has held since October 1995. Madonna is joining Travelers Group Inc as a vice chairman.</p>
<p>The largest professional services firm said Sharman, 53, will remain U.K. senior partner, a position he has held for the past three years.</p>
</text>
